  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "HfNbTaTiZr is an equiatomic alloy examined in the as-cast state.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cast equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr exhibits 8–16% room-temperature tensile ductility.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cast equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr has a yield strength of 163–530 MPa at 1000 °C at strain rates of 10^-4–10^-2 s^-1.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HfNbTaTiZr has inadequate oxidation resistance for high-temperature use in air.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "An anti-oxidation coating is a relevant intervention for enabling high-temperature use of this refractory alloy family in air.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coating should specifically be a thin, adherent, alumina-forming aluminide coating.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Physical vapor deposition or pack aluminization can be used to apply the proposed coating to HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed coating is intended to protect HfNbTaTiZr during approximately 100 hours of exposure to air at 1000 °C.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective effect is expected under static or cyclic loading at strain rates of 10^-4–10^-2 s^-1.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coating will form a continuous, dense, and adherent Al2O3 surface scale.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alumina scale will act as a physical diffusion barrier.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The diffusion barrier will reduce oxygen ingress and prevent internal oxidation of HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A thin surface coating will leave the bulk microstructure of HfNbTaTiZr largely unaffected.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preserving the bulk microstructure will preserve the alloy's useful mechanical performance.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to uncoated HfNbTaTiZr, coated specimens will show markedly less oxide-scale formation and lower oxygen uptake at 1000 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After coating and exposure, room-temperature tensile ductility will remain within 8–16%.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After coating and exposure, yield strength at 1000 °C will remain within 163–530 MPa under the stated strain-rate range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated cast HfNbTaTiZr undergoes rapid oxidation in high-temperature air.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Coating integrity under repeated thermal cycling or exposure beyond 100 hours is uncertain.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
